Conceptual Reflection: Hot Reload vs. Hot Restart
Hot Reload: Injects updated code changes directly into the running Dart Virtual Machine (VM) without losing the current application state. It allows developers to instantly preview UI tweaks and minor logic updates within sub-seconds.
Hot Restart: Fully destroys and rebuilds the Dart VM state, clearing memory and resetting app runtime back to its initial entry point (main()). It is required when modifying global variables, app initialization logic, or static fields.
